  "grammar_observation": {
    "target_language": "cath fach, cath wen, cath ddu; draig fach, draig goch. Ond: ci bach, ci gwyn, ci du. b → f; g → ∅; d → dd.",
    "bridge_language": "With many singular feminine nouns, a following adjective soft-mutates: cath + bach → cath fach, cath + gwyn → cath wen, and cath + du → cath ddu. The masculine contrast keeps ci bach, ci gwyn, ci du."
  },
